# Machine-local state the release clone shares with the live install.
# One path per line, relative to the repo root. `dir/` is a directory
# (created in the shared checkout if absent); anything else is a file that must
# already exist there.
# state/ carries the pbcom-pull.lock / pbcom-link.lock singleton locks: the code
# takes them from REPO_ROOT, so this link is what keeps that protection.
pbcom-driver/.env
pbcom-driver/state/
pbcom-driver/binding.json
